[[File:Chainsawman.jpg|upright|thumb|Cover of the first {{Transliteration|ja|[[tankōbon]]}}, released in Japan by [[Shueisha]] on March 4, 2019]]
''[[Chainsaw Man]]'' is a Japanese [[manga]] series written and illustrated by [[Tatsuki Fujimoto]]. The series' first part, the {{Nihongo|"Public Safety Arc"|公安編|Kōan-hen}}, covered in the first 97 chapters, ran in [[Shueisha]]'s [[Shōnen manga|{{Transliteration|ja|shōnen}} manga]] anthology ''[[Weekly Shōnen Jump]]'' from December 3, 2018,<ref>{{cite web|last=Ressler|first=Karen|title=Shonen Jump Magazine Launches 3 New Manga in December|url=http://www.animenewsnetwork.com/news/2018-11-25/shonen-jump-magazine-launches-3-new-manga-in-december/.139892|website=[[Anime News Network]]|access-date=September 14, 2019|date=November 25, 2018|archive-date=May 3, 2021|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210503160935/https://www.animenewsnetwork.com/news/2018-11-25/shonen-jump-magazine-launches-3-new-manga-in-december/.139892|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|script-title=ja:「ファイアパンチ」の藤本タツキが描くダークヒーロー譚、ジャンプで始動|url=https://natalie.mu/comic/news/310548|website=[[Comic Natalie]]|publisher=Natasha, Inc|access-date=July 8, 2020|language=ja|date=December 3, 2018|archive-date=December 7, 2020|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20201207214552/https://natalie.mu/comic/news/310548|url-status=live}}</ref> to December 14, 2020;<ref>{{cite web|last=Hodgkins|first=Crystalyn|title=Chainsaw Man Manga Ends on December 14 With 'Important Announcement'|url=https://www.animenewsnetwork.com/news/2020-12-06/chainsaw-man-manga-ends-on-december-14-with-important-announcement/.167132|website=[[Anime News Network]]|access-date=December 6, 2020|date=December 6, 2020|archive-date=February 17, 2021|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210217192054/https://www.animenewsnetwork.com/news/2020-12-06/chainsaw-man-manga-ends-on-december-14-with-important-announcement/.167132|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|script-title=ja:漫画『チェンソーマン』第1部完結、第2部がジャンプ+に掲載へ TVアニメ化など新情報続々|url=https://www.oricon.co.jp/news/2179155/full/|website=[[Oricon News]]|access-date=December 13, 2020|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20201213222330/https://www.oricon.co.jp/news/2179155/full/|archive-date=December 13, 2020|language=ja|date=December 14, 2020|url-status=live}}</ref> following the series' conclusion in ''Weekly Shōnen Jump'', a second part was announced to start on Shueisha's ''[[Shōnen Jump+]]'' online magazine.<ref name="2nd-part">{{cite web|last=Hodgkins|first=Crystalyn|title=Chainsaw Man Manga Ends '1st Part,' '2nd Part' to Serialize on Shonen Jump+|url=https://www.animenewsnetwork.com/news/2020-12-13/chainsaw-man-manga-ends-1st-part-2nd-part-to-serialize-on-shonen-jump/.167381|website=[[Anime News Network]]|access-date=December 13, 2020|date=December 13, 2020|archive-date=May 3, 2021|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210503160917/https://www.animenewsnetwork.com/news/2020-12-13/chainsaw-man-manga-ends-1st-part-2nd-part-to-serialize-on-shonen-jump/.167381|url-status=live}}</ref> On December 19, 2020, it was announced that the second part, the {{Nihongo|"School Arc"|学校編|Gakkō-hen}}, would feature Denji going to school.<ref>{{cite web|last=Hodgkins|first=Crystalyn|title=Chainsaw Man Manga's '2nd Part' to Feature 'School Arc'|url=https://www.animenewsnetwork.com/daily-briefs/2020-12-19/chainsaw-man-manga-2nd-part-to-feature-school-arc/.167630|website=[[Anime News Network]]|access-date=December 19, 2020|date=December 19, 2020|archive-date=April 26, 2021|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210426130812/https://www.animenewsnetwork.com/daily-briefs/2020-12-19/chainsaw-man-manga-2nd-part-to-feature-school-arc/.167630|url-status=live}}</ref> The second part was serialized from July 13, 2022,<ref>{{cite web|last=Hodgkins|first=Crystalyn|title=Chainsaw Man Manga's 2nd Part Launches on Shonen Jump+ on July 13|url=https://www.animenewsnetwork.com/news/2022-06-20/chainsaw-man-manga-2nd-part-launches-on-shonen-jump-on-july-13/.186863|website=[[Anime News Network]]|access-date=June 20, 2022|date=June 20, 2022|archive-date=June 20, 2022|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220620105920/https://www.animenewsnetwork.com/news/2022-06-20/chainsaw-man-manga-2nd-part-launches-on-shonen-jump-on-july-13/.186863|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|script-title=ja:藤本タツキ「チェンソーマン」第二部の連載がジャンプ+でスタート|url=https://natalie.mu/comic/news/485195|website=[[Comic Natalie]]|publisher=Natasha, Inc|access-date=July 14, 2022|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220712151327/https://natalie.mu/comic/news/485195|archive-date=July 12, 2022|language=ja|date=July 13, 2022|url-status=live}}</ref> to March 25, 2026.<ref>{{cite web|last=Mateo|first=Alex|title=Chainsaw Man Manga's 2nd Part Ends on March 24|url=https://www.animenewsnetwork.com/news/2026-03-10/chainsaw-man-manga-2nd-part-ends-on-march-24/.235143|website=[[Anime News Network]]|access-date=March 10, 2026|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260310171751/https://www.animenewsnetwork.com/news/2026-03-10/chainsaw-man-manga-2nd-part-ends-on-march-24/.235143|archive-date=March 10, 2026|date=March 10, 2026|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|script-title=ja:漫画『チェンソーマン』第2部完結 コミックス完結24巻は6月4日発売|url=https://www.oricon.co.jp/news/2444396/full/|website=[[Oricon News]]|access-date=March 25, 2026|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260325022714/https://www.oricon.co.jp/news/2444396/full/|archive-date=March 25, 2026|language=ja|date=March 25, 2026|url-status=live}}</ref> Shueisha collected its chapters in 24 {{Transliteration|ja|[[tankōbon]]}} volumes, released from March 4, 2019, to June 4, 2026.<ref name="JPvol1"/><ref name="JPvol24"/>

In North America, [[Viz Media]] published the series' first two chapters on their ''[[Weekly Shonen Jump (American magazine)|Weekly Shonen Jump]]'' digital magazine for its "Jump Start" initiative.<ref name="vizpreview">{{cite web|last=Ressler|first=Karen|title=Viz's Shonen Jump to Preview Chainsaw Man by Fire Punch's Fujimoto|url=http://www.animenewsnetwork.com/news/2018-11-26/viz-shonen-jump-to-preview-chainsaw-man-by-fire-punch-fujimoto/.139986|website=[[Anime News Network]]|access-date=September 14, 2019|date=November 26, 2018|archive-date=March 4, 2021|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210304002407/https://www.animenewsnetwork.com/news/2018-11-26/viz-shonen-jump-to-preview-chainsaw-man-by-fire-punch-fujimoto/.139986|url-status=live}}</ref><ref name="VIZ-SJ-ANN"/> The series was then published on the ''Shonen Jump'' digital platform after the cancellation of ''Weekly Shonen Jump''.<ref name="VIZ-SJ-ANN">{{cite web|last=Ressler|first=Karen|title=Viz's Shonen Jump Adds Haikyu!!, Demon Slayer, More to Simulpublishing Lineup|url=http://www.animenewsnetwork.com/news/2018-12-10/viz-shonen-jump-adds-haikyu-demon-slayer-more-to-simulpublishing-lineup/.140628|website=[[Anime News Network]]|access-date=September 14, 2019|date=December 10, 2018|archive-date=June 30, 2019|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190630105249/https://www.animenewsnetwork.com/news/2018-12-10/viz-shonen-jump-adds-haikyu-demon-slayer-more-to-simulpublishing-lineup/.140628|url-status=live}}</ref> Shueisha also simulpublished the series in English on the app and website ''[[Manga Plus]]'' starting in January 2019.<ref>{{cite web|last=Morrissy|first=Kim|title=Everything You Need to Know about MANGA Plus by Shueisha|url=http://www.animenewsnetwork.com/feature/2019-01-27/everything-you-need-to-know-about-manga-plus-by-shueisha/.142401|website=[[Anime News Network]]|access-date=September 14, 2019|date=January 27, 2019|archive-date=August 6, 2019|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190806080607/https://www.animenewsnetwork.com/feature/2019-01-27/everything-you-need-to-know-about-manga-plus-by-shueisha/.142401|url-status=live}}</ref> In February 2020, Viz Media announced the digital and print release of the manga.<ref>{{cite web|last=Sherman|first=Jennifer|title=Viz Licenses Remina, Moriarty the Patriot, Fly Me to the Moon, More Manga|url=https://www.animenewsnetwork.com/news/2020-02-14/viz-licenses-remina-moriarty-the-patriot-fly-me-to-the-moon-more-manga/.156474|website=[[Anime News Network]]|access-date=February 14, 2020|date=February 14, 2020|archive-date=October 28, 2020|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20201028061935/https://www.animenewsnetwork.com/news/2020-02-14/viz-licenses-remina-moriarty-the-patriot-fly-me-to-the-moon-more-manga/.156474|url-status=live}}</ref> The first volume was released on October 6, 2020.<ref name="Vizvol1"/> As of March 3, 2026, 20 volumes have been released.<ref name="Vizvol20"/>
